{"title":"MET Manta 3 Aero Road Helmet is Already World Championship-Winning, Plus 6W Faster","link":"https://bikerumor.com/met-manta-3-aero-road-helmet-is-already-world-championship-winning-plus-6w-faster/","date":1794509977000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/MET-Manta-3-aero-road-helmet-of-choice-of-2025-World-Champion-Tadej-Pogacar-and-2026-World-Champ-Brandon-McNulty_photos-by-Sprint-Cycling-Agency-1536x1024.jpg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"&lt;i&gt;(Photos by Sprint Cycling Agency/MET)&lt;/I&gt;\" /></p>\n<p>We already spotted MET’s new Manta 3 aero road helmet on UAE women’s and men’ pro heads in the World Tour this season, from last year’s World Champ <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/?s=Poga%C4%8Dar\" target=\"_blank\">Tadej Pogačar</a> to this year’s <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/brandon-mcnulty-wins-road-worlds-ending-a-33-year-u-s-drought/\" target=\"_blank\">new champ Brandon McNulty</a>. But now you can buy one. And MET has shared all the tech details about what makes their core road racing helmet faster, and safer, than ever.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>MET Manta 3 aero road racing helmet</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view.jpg\" alt=\"2026 MET Manta 3 aero road racing helmet\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_ront-view-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a><figcaption><i>(All photos/MET)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Last week MET unveiled the more affordable no-carbon <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/met-trenta-2-road-helmet-maxes-airflow-at-same-weight-but-25-lower-price-vs-carbon/\" target=\"_blank\">Trenta 2</a> version of their airflow-maxed road helmet. But if speed is your priority on the bike, it’s time to look at the new Manta 3 on the aero road side.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Manta 3 officially broke cover this season at Milan-Sanremo in March, where Pogačar sprinted to that crash-tattered &amp; bloody win ahead of Tom Pidcock. Not a bad first race for the new MET lid. Did a new aero helmet help him win? It likely didn’t hurt, if MET’s wind tunnel claims are right.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster-inside-the-Tube-MET-wind-tunnel.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1125\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster-inside-the-Tube-MET-wind-tunnel.jpg\" alt=\"2026 MET Manta 3 aero road racing helmet: inside MET's Tube wind tunnel\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster-inside-the-Tube-MET-wind-tunnel.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster-inside-the-Tube-MET-wind-tunnel-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster-inside-the-Tube-MET-wind-tunnel-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster-inside-the-Tube-MET-wind-tunnel-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster-inside-the-Tube-MET-wind-tunnel-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster-inside-the-Tube-MET-wind-tunnel-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster-inside-the-Tube-MET-wind-tunnel-1600x900.jpg 1600w\" /></a><figcaption>testing inside MET’s own <em>Tube</em> wind tunnel</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>They explain that at the 50km/hr speeds that road racers see, aero drag starts to become a really big obstacle to overcome. So they spent years refining the Manta, and came out saving an extra 6W over <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/met-update-the-manta-mips-road-helmet-with-smokin-hot-aero-design/\" target=\"_blank\">the gen 2 helmet</a> with this new design. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_new-F1-inspired-Double-Deck-rear-vent-deflectors.jpg\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1125\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_new-F1-inspired-Double-Deck-rear-vent-deflectors.jpg\" alt=\"2026 MET Manta 3 aero road racing helmet: Double Deck rear vet deflectors\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_new-F1-inspired-Double-Deck-rear-vent-deflectors.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_new-F1-inspired-Double-Deck-rear-vent-deflectors-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_new-F1-inspired-Double-Deck-rear-vent-deflectors-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_new-F1-inspired-Double-Deck-rear-vent-deflectors-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_new-F1-inspired-Double-Deck-rear-vent-deflectors-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_new-F1-inspired-Double-Deck-rear-vent-deflectors-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_new-F1-inspired-Double-Deck-rear-vent-deflectors-1600x900.jpg 1600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Plus – thanks to the revised three main forward-facing vents design, lower-profile MIPS Air Node system inside, revised internal channeling, and a new F1-inspired pair of Double Deck air deflectors at the back – the new Manta 3 promises a 10% improvement in ventilation, as well.</p>\n\n\n\n<h4><em>Old vs. New aero shaping</em></h4>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_white-new-vs-red-old.jpg\"><img width=\"1800\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_white-new-vs-red-old.jpg\" alt=\"new MET Manta 3 aero road helmet vs. old Manta 2 \" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_white-new-vs-red-old.jpg 1800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_white-new-vs-red-old-297x165.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_white-new-vs-red-old-1536x853.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_white-new-vs-red-old-120x67.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_white-new-vs-red-old-768x427.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_white-new-vs-red-old-1600x889.jpg 1600w\" /></a><figcaption>new Manta 3 <i>(white)</i>  vs. old Manta 2 <i>(red)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>MET describes the new Manta 3 as being a bit shorter and smoother than the Manta 2. That’s especially evident in the shift of its ‘tail’ further back and lower, and fewer sharp edges. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top.jpg\"><img width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top.jpg\" alt=\"2026 MET Manta 3 aero road racing helmet: silver top\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top.jpg 2400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-top-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The obvious move from two to three main front vents is visually distinct, of course. But the most significant change is the loss of the top vent, as we’ve seen almost every modern aero helmet remove any edges or openings from the top of all their latest designs to reduce drag.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3>Tech details</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-side.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-side-1536x1152.jpg\" alt=\"2026 MET Manta 3 aero road racing helmet: silver side\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-side-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-side-297x223.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-side-120x90.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-side-768x576.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-side-2048x1536.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-side-1200x900.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-angled.jpg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-angled-1536x1152.jpg\" alt=\"2026 MET Manta 3 aero road racing helmet: silver angled rear\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-angled-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-angled-297x223.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-angled-120x90.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-angled-768x576.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-angled-2048x1536.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_silver-angled-1200x900.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>wind tunnel-optimized aero road helmet</li>\n\n\n\n<li>MET ranks it as “the fastest” in benchmark tests in their own “<em>Tube</em>” wind tunnel</li>\n\n\n\n<li>in-mold EPS construction with full-wrap 3-piece polycarbonate shell</li>\n\n\n\n<li>MIPS Air Node lightweight anti-rotation protection</li>\n\n\n\n<li>protection optimized from analysis of 142 real crash-damaged helmets worn by UAE Team Emirates between 2019-2025</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Coolmax integrated pads</li>\n\n\n\n<li>two side vents function as sunglasses ports</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Double Deck rear vent air deflectors</li>\n\n\n\n<li>dial- &amp; height-adjustable Safe-T Orbital Fit System</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Air Lite straps with adjustable under-ear hardware</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Virginia Tech Helmet Lab 5-star safety rating</li>\n\n\n\n<li>CE | US | AS-NZ safety certifications</li>\n\n\n\n<li>3 sizes (S 52-56cm, M 56-58cm &amp; L 58-61cm)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>250g claimed weight (<em>CE, size M</em>) </li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3>MET Manta 3 – Pricing, options &amp; availability</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors.jpg\"><img width=\"2400\" height=\"1600\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors.jpg\" alt=\"2026 MET Manta 3 aero road racing helmet: colors\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors.jpg 2400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-MET-Manta-3-aero-road-racing-helmet-is-6W-faster_colors-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The new redesigned MET Manta 3 aero road bike helmet sells for $375 / 330€, including a soft helmet bag for storage. It is available now in six relatively low-key colors. Pick from all-black, all-white, white with black logos and EPS, dark grey, light silver, or a red-to-black fade.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em><a href=\"https://www.met-helmets.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MET-hemets.com</a></em></p>","author":"Cory Benson","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/met-manta-3-aero-road-helmet-is-already-world-championship-winning-plus-6w-faster/#comments","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"b48f265176f5c32a51aacba89da050fd9c5880525c44aae8116a382e77102fb5","category":"Cycling"}